|36|2096||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11044647</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hochhauser</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Informed consent and patient's rights documents: a right, a rite, or a rewrite?</article-title><source>Ethics Behav</source><year>1999</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Ethics Behav||9|1||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11657485</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jenkins</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Fallowfield</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reasons for accepting or declining to participate in randomized trials for cancer therapy</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2000</year><volume>82</volume><supplement>11</supplement><fpage>1783</fpage><lpage>1788</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||82|1783||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10839291</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jenkins</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fallowfield</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Souhami</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sawtell</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How do doctors explain RCTs to their patients</article-title><source>Eur J Cancer</source><year>1999</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1187</fpage><lpage>1193</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Cancer||35|1187||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10615228</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Llewellyn-Thomas</